      "updated_at": "2026-09-28T08:50:16Z",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Thanks for reporting. By reading the logs, it seems a fee rate of 1.009 was passed as the `-maxfeerate` for the wallet, and then we attempted to submit a tx with the exact 1.009 fee rate. The check is that any fee rate above that should be rejected for creation and submission.\nIt seems somehow the transaction ended up with a fee rate higher than what was intended, and the wallet rightfully rejects it.\n\nMy suspect is https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/29278#discussion_r3776197834, because this test on the boundary, and since the wallet may falsely reject, this occur.\n\nA simple fix would be to not test at the boundary, but that just hides the issue.\n\ncc @polespinasa @furszy ",
      "user": {
        "login": "ismaelsadeeq",
        "id": 48946461,
        "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQ4OTQ2NDYx",
